  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Mitigate the risk of river flooding in Kindu city, Mikelenge, Alunguli and Kasuku Communes</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Since 2016, increased rainfall has been observed in Maniema during the rainy season. Every year, the population of Kindu and the Ka&#xef;lo territory fears disaster due to river and rainwater flooding, which leads to loss of life, the destruction of livestock, homes, and basic social infrastructure (hospitals, schools, markets, water sources or wells, roads), as well as fields and fish ponds. The consequences are numerous: increased poverty (increased vulnerability), food insecurity, malnutrition among children under five and breastfeeding women, an increase in waterborne diseases, etc.

Since 2022, with the support of the StartNetwork through the StartReady mechanism, within the framework of the DRF program, and thanks to the developed river flood model (JBA), projects have been undertaken to support the population in mitigating the likely impacts and contributing to rescue efforts.&quot; human lives. In 2023 and 2024, the model was activated and actions were taken.</narrative>
  </description>
